<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ancient Olympic Games</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">776 BCE–4th century CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The ancient Olympic Games were a religious and athletic festival held every four years at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olympia">Olympia</a> in honour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a>, traditionally from 776 BCE. Free Greek men competed in running, wrestling, boxing, the pentathlon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> races, and a sacred truce protected travellers to the festival. Elis organised the games through its officials, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellanodikai">Hellanodikai</a>, and they continued under Roman rule until the late 4th century CE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ancient-olympic-games.jpg" alt="Ancient Olympic Games" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bgabel · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GR-olympia-palaestra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
